==Acquisition==
*This mod can be acquired by attaining the rank of '''Maxim''' under {{Faction|Arbiters of Hexis}}, or the rank of '''Partner''' under {{Faction|The Perrin Sequence}}, and spending {{sc|25,000}} to purchase.

==Notes==
* Grants {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''75%''' electricity damage '''and''' {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''75%''' electricity status damage.
** '''Electricity damage''' bonus is additive with electricity damage sources, such as {{M|Stormbringer}}. However, unlike modded electricity damage, this bonus is '''not''' counted in the "electricity damage bonuses" portion of the status damage calculation (bug), and therefore does not add any damage to electricity statuses. See [[Electricity Damage#Damage_Over_Time|Electricity Damage]] for the status damage formula.
** '''Electricity status damage''' bonus stacks additively with status damage sources, such as {{M|Rifle Elementalist}}. The bonus only applies to electricity procs, but works on both the guaranteed electric procs from this augment and natural electric procs from the weapon.
**This behavior is '''after''' the U38.6 patch, which was supposed to fix the status damage calculation.
* Shooting through multiple arcspheres '''will''' grant additional guaranteed electric procs and electricity damage, but will '''not''' grant additional electricity status damage. 
* Projectiles only need to pass through the {{A|Arcsphere}}'s electric field in order to gain the bonus, not the arcsphere object itself.
** Standing within the electric field will trigger the bonus on all shots fired.
** Non-projectile (hitscan, beam, etc) weapons can trigger the effect as well, whether by shooting through the sphere or standing within it.
*Visit [[Buffing Fields]] to learn more about the mechanic and targets (weapons, abilities, other) which can benefit from this mod.
*Uniquely the added electricity damage is added to some explosive weapons (e.g. [[acceltra]]) but the guaranteed electric status is not.

==Bugs==
* The electricity damage granted from this augment does not directly increase electricity proc damage, like sources of electricity damage normally would. Instead, a separate status damage bonus is applied.
** This behavior is '''after''' the U38.6 patch, which was supposed to fix the status damage calculation.
* With Conductive Sphere equipped, {{A|Null Star}} will not seek out enemies while the player is standing within an arcsphere field, or while an arcsphere is between the player and an enemy. 
**This does not occur when using {{M|Neutron Star}} to send out remaining stars by recasting the ability. However, Nullstars will still not gain the electricity buff when moving through an arcsphere.
*Find out more in [[Buffing Fields#Bugs]].

